  ('gcid:calligraphy_lesson','location','location','active',ARRAY['Nib','Copperplate','Broad-edge pen','Flourishing','Letterform','Ascender and descender','Ink viscosity','Pointed pen','Monoline script','Orthography']::text[],'["Beginner pointed pen calligraphy workshops", "Broad-edge/italic calligraphy group classes", "Modern brush lettering courses", "Wedding suite addressing and envelope calligraphy", "Private one-on-one calligraphy instruction", "Children''s calligraphy summer camps", "Corporate team-building calligraphy events", "Online virtual calligraphy lessons", "Specialty script courses (Spencerian, Gothic, Uncial)", "Supply starter kit sales bundled with instruction"]'::jsonb,ARRAY['Business must collect and remit applicable state and local sales tax on taxable goods sold (e.g., supply kits, tools) per each state''s Department of Revenue requirements.','If operating as a home-based studio, the instructor must comply with local zoning ordinances and may need a home occupation permit before hosting students on-site.','Gift cards and class credit sold to students are subject to federal CARD Act provisions limiting expiration and inactivity fees if issued as stored-value instruments.','Advertising claims (e.g., ''award-winning,'' ''certified instructor'') must be truthful and substantiated under FTC guidelines to avoid deceptive advertising violations.','If classes are offered to minors, the business must obtain signed parental consent forms and maintain appropriate supervision ratios per local childcare regulations where applicable.','ADA Title III requires public-facing places of education and accommodation to provide reasonable accessibility for individuals with disabilities, including physical studio access.','Online course sales across state lines may trigger economic nexus obligations for sales tax collection in states where the business exceeds revenue or transaction thresholds.','Instructors who incorporate their business must comply with applicable s