  ('gcid:cannabis_club','location','location','active',ARRAY['dispensary','flower','concentrate','edibles','terpenes','cannabinoids','THC/CBD ratio','indica/sativa/hybrid','budtender','COA (Certificate of Analysis)']::text[],'["Retail cannabis flower sales", "Cannabis concentrate and extract sales", "Edibles and infused product sales", "Topicals and tinctures sales", "Pre-roll and convenience product sales", "Member/loyalty program enrollment", "Budtender product consultation", "Online ordering and curbside pickup", "Cannabis accessories and paraphernalia retail", "Educational sessions on responsible consumption"]'::jsonb,ARRAY['Age verification is federally mandated by state law: all customers must present valid government-issued ID confirming they are 21+ for recreational use, or 18+ with a valid medical cannabis card where applicable.','Cannabis remains a Schedule I controlled substance under the federal Controlled Substances Act (CSA); clubs operate exclusively under state and local licensing frameworks and may not ship products across state lines.','Advertising restrictions vary by state but generally prohibit targeting individuals under 21, advertising on platforms frequented by minors, and making unsubstantiated health claims about cannabis products.','All cannabis products sold must be tested by a state-licensed third-party laboratory and accompanied by a Certificate of Analysis (COA) disclosing potency, pesticides, heavy metals, and microbial contaminants.','Seed-to-sale tracking is required in most legal states (e.g., via Metrc or BioTrackTHC) to ensure full supply-chain traceability and regulatory compliance.','Packaging and labeling laws require child-resistant containers, clear THC/CBD content disclosures, universal cannabis warning symbols, and prohibition of packaging designed to appeal to minors.','Club operators must hold all required state and municipal business licenses (retailer license, local conditional use permit) and are subject to regular in