anations, and quality follow-up encourage repeat use and referrals"]'::jsonb,'["CLIA certification status and CAP accreditation clearly visible in GBP profile and on-site", "Complete and accurate business information (hours, phone, address, website) with no discrepancies across citations", "High review volume and rating (4.5+ stars); professional, responsive review replies from management", "Local citation consistency on industry directories (LabCorp, Quest Diagnostics networks, state health department listings)", "On-page content emphasizing CLIA compliance, turnaround times, accepted insurance, and available test menu", "Local link profile from healthcare networks, employer partnerships, and hospital/clinic referral relationships"]'::jsonb,ARRAY['Quick turnaround time','Professional phlebotomists','Easy online appointment booking','Clear and timely results','Insurance accepted','Minimal wait time','Knowledgeable staff','Clean and sterile facility','Fast results delivery','Friendly check-in process']::text[],ARRAY['What tests does our lab offer and when are they recommended?','Understanding your lab results: how to read common blood panels','CLIA certification and accreditation: what it means for patient safety','Fasting requirements and specimen collection best practices','Turnaround times for common tests and rush options','Insurance coverage and out-of-pocket costs for laboratory services','Occupational health testing and employer screening programs']::text[],'["Current CLIA certification and accreditation badge (CAP, AABB, or state equivalent)", "Lab Director credentials (MD, DO, PhD) with state licensure prominently featured", "Years in operation and patient volume (e.g., ''serving 50,000+ patients annually'')", "Professional memberships (ASCP, AAL, state laboratory associations)", "Quality metrics (turnaround time guarantees, accuracy rates, customer satisfaction scores)", "Continuing education and regulatory compliance documentation"]'::jsonb,'{"profile_comp